.SH NAME
.PP
auto-ldap-lookup - Look up users on a remote LDAP or AD server

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-ldap-lookup [username]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
username    Username of an existing user
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-ldap-lookup
command attempts to look up a user by username on the configured
LDAP or AD server.  The system must already be configured as an
LDAP or AD client, e.g. using auto-ldap-client-setup(8).

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-ldap-lookup jsmith
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-ldap-client-setup(8)

